{
  "an5.57:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 5.57 ",
  "an5.57:0.2": "6. Hindrances ",
  "an5.57:0.3": "Subjects for Regular Reviewing ",
  "an5.57:1.1": "“Mendicants, a woman or a man, a layperson or a renunciate should often review these five subjects. ",
  "an5.57:1.2": "What five? ",
  "an5.57:1.3": "‘I am liable to grow old, I am not exempt from old age.’ A woman or a man, a layperson or a renunciate should often review this. ",
  "an5.57:1.4": "‘I am liable to get sick, I am not exempt from sickness.’ … ",
  "an5.57:1.5": "‘I am liable to die, I am not exempt from death.’ … ",
  "an5.57:1.6": "‘I must be parted and separated from all I hold dear and beloved.’ … ",
  "an5.57:1.7": "‘I am the owner of my deeds and heir to my deeds. Deeds are my womb, my relative, and my refuge. ",
  "an5.57:1.8": "I shall be the heir of whatever deeds I do, whether good or bad.’ ",
  "an5.57:1.9": "A woman or a man, a layperson or a renunciate should often review this. ",
  "an5.57:2.1": "What is the advantage for a woman or a man, a layperson or a renunciate of often reviewing this: ‘I am liable to grow old, I am not exempt from old age’? ",
  "an5.57:2.2": "There are sentient beings who, intoxicated with the vanity of youth, do bad things by way of body, speech, and mind. ",
  "an5.57:2.3": "Reviewing this subject often, they entirely give up the vanity of youth, or at least reduce it. ",
  "an5.57:2.4": "This is the advantage for a woman or a man, a layperson or a renunciate of often reviewing t